  Rule: M17. Variants are joined by a shared ClinVar VariationID, or by finding one row of a variant classifications table, and by no other code
    decisions/variant-identity.md, rows "join by ID (R12)", "join through the table (R13)", "how a version finds its row", "left alone" and "computed identity"; decisions/performance.md, row "page-read tables, current versions only"; decisions/variant-record.md, row "computed identity".
    R12 joins two variants whose current versions carry one ClinVar VariationID, the digits alone. R13 joins two
    variants whose current versions find one row of one version of a variant classifications table. A version that
    carries a VariationID finds the row of that variation through the ID alone, and its HGVS expression is not read; a
    version that carries none finds the row that holds its expression (M4). The classification plays no part: the join
    is identity. A pair that shares an ID is R12's alone, so no pair has two justifications; a pair whose versions carry
    different IDs is joined by neither, whatever expressions they hold; and a variant whose expression is on more than
    one row is left alone, rows being counted as distinct row subjects over every version held. The reasons are in
    decisions/variant-identity.md; no other code is compared, because an HGVS expression written on two transcript
    versions is two expressions, and only a table says they are one variant.

    Ivo's table holds ClinVar's rows of two variations of MLH1, 90011 and 90012, 90011 found by its expression on each
    of two transcript versions. Each example opens a new pod for Ivo with it and enters its own entry, so that no
    example's variants join another's.

